{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>It is removed</b> — 2, as in \"the fat is removed.\" And from the time the daily offering is removed — to say that from the time the daily offering was removed, all fat was removed, for in its merit blessing is sent into all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The word הוסר appears twice with the sense 'is removed/has been removed'; Ba'al HaTurim links the occurrence in our verse to the phrase about the daily offering (tamid), preserving his terse juxtaposition without resolving which specific second occurrence he cites."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:50.422074081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}